    caption: Clay impression of a cylinder seal with monstrous lions and
      lion-headed eagles, Mesopotamia, Uruk Period (4100–3000 BC). Louvre
      Museum.
  - file: Limestone_foundation_peg_of_Lugal-kisal-si,_from_Uruk,_Iraq._C._2380_BCE._Pergamon_Museum.jpg
    role: inline
    section: early-dynastic-akkadian-ur-iii-and-old-babylonian-period
    caption: Foundation peg of [[ Lugal-kisalsi ]], king of Uruk, Ur and Kish,
      circa 2380 BC. The inscription reads "For (the goddess) [[ Namma | nammu
      ]], wife of (the god) [[ An | anu ]], Lugalkisalsi, King of Uruk, King
      of Ur, erected this temple of Namma". [[ Pergamon Museum ]] VA 4855.[[
      ^2 ]]
  - file: Tablet_of_Sin-Gamil_of_Uruk.jpg
    role: inline
