      to the reign of Ur-Nammu
  - file: Gebel_el-Arak_Knife_ivory_handle_(front_top_part_detail).jpg
    role: full
    section: political-history
    caption: A Mesopotamian king as [[ Master of Animals ]] on the [[ Gebel
      el-Arak Knife ]] (c. 3300–3200 BC, [[ Abydos, Egypt ]]), a work
      indicating [[ Egypt-Mesopotamia relations | egyptmesopotamia-relations
      ]] and showing the early influence of Mesopotamia on [[ Egypt ]] and the
      state of Mesopotamian royal iconography in the Uruk period. [[ Louvre
      ]].[[ ^23 ]][[ ^24 ]]
  - file: Uruk_King-Priest_3300_BCE_portrait_detail.jpg
