    width: 577
    height: 599
    caption: "Mesopotamia in the 2nd millennium BC. From north to south: Nineveh,
      Qattara (or Karana), Dūr-Katlimmu, Assur, Arrapha, Terqa, Nuzi, Mari,
      Eshnunna, Dur-Kurigalzu, Der, Sippar, Babylon, Kish, Susa, Borsippa,
      Nippur, Isin, Uruk, Larsa and Ur."
  - file: Male_deity_pouring_a_life-giving_water_from_a_vessel._Facade_of_Inanna_Temple_at_Uruk,_Iraq._15th_century_BC._The_Pergamon_Museum.jpg
